  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn></math> droplets of water of surface tension <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>07</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. having same radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> each, combine to from a single drop. In the process the released surface energy is-</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Take</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
